.TH QUANUXCTL-QUERY 1 "March 2026" "QuanuX" "QuanuX Control Manual"
.SH NAME
quanuxctl-query \- Manage Analytical Extensions (Validate & Estimate SQL)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quanuxctl query validate
[\fB--target\fR \fIbq\fR]
\fIsql_file\fR
.PP
.B quanuxctl query estimate
[\fB--target\fR \fIbq\fR]
\fIsql_file\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quanuxctl query
exposes the QuanuX-Annex Transpiler for user-facing backtest validation against the warm analytical tier (e.g. Google BigQuery). It acts as an AST interceptor boundary ensuring strict SQL constraints are met prior to cluster execution.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B validate \fIsql_file\fR
Parses the local DuckDB SQL query inside the given file against the internal Allowed/Banned matrix without hitting the network API. Checks exactly match Phase 1 structural policies.
.br
\fBExit Codes:\fR
.br
.B 0\fR - Synthesis and rules validation passed.
.br
.B 1\fR - Syntax verification blocked (TranspilationError). Prints explicit rejection reason.

.TP
.B estimate \fIsql_file\fR
Transpiles the AST and hits the target BigQuery Dry-Run API. Returns exact bytes-billed output, payload formatting metrics, and expected latency tiers to the operator prior to commitment. Employs mock inference if GCP pipeline keys are unset in CI/CD limits.
.br
\fBExit Codes:\fR
.br
.B 0\fR - Dry-run completed successfully and outputs structural estimates.
.br
.B 1\fR - Network failure or Phase 1 synthesis bounds triggered.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-target \fIengine\fR
Specifies the analytical engine target. Currently defaults to \fBbq\fR (BigQuery).

.SH EXAMPLES
.B quanuxctl query validate my_backtest.sql --target bq
.PP
.B quanuxctl query estimate my_backtest.sql
